@startuml

start

:Thermal management controller operates as state machine within hard real-time RTOS;
fork
:Govern multi-zone PWM fans;
fork again
:Govern liquid-cooling loops;
end fork

:Primary control task scheduled from high-priority queue;
:Continuously monitor temperature sensor data protected by mutex;

if (Reading > threshold?) then (yes)
  :Associated ISR triggers emergency cooling state;
  :Initialize primary fan array;
  :Validate operation via dedicated watchdog;

  if (Detect fan fault?) then (yes)
    fork
      :Engage redundant backup unit;
    fork again
      :Concurrent lower-priority task monitors coolant flow via CAN-connected sensor;
      if (Insufficient flow?) then (yes)
        :Trigger replenishment from reserve system;
      else (no)
      end if
    end fork
  else (no)
  end if

  if (Temperature continues to rise?) then (yes)
    :Indicate critical fault;
    :Execute exponential backoff;
    :Re-initialize backup cooling plan;
    repeat
    :Iterate through ring buffer of recent sensor data within closed-loop FADEC-style control law;
    :Dynamically adjust cooling intensity;
    repeat while(Core equipment remains within safe operating range?) is(no)
  else (no)
  end if

else (no)
end if

fork
  :System health monitor task driven by periodic timer interrupts;
  :Perform bounded-retry checks on PMIC and BMS;
  :Guarantee other functional modules remain unaffected;
fork again
  :Secure all critical telemetry packets by CRC;
end fork

stop

@enduml
